commitResults.messageBody:
According to the Java Coding Guide, Lambda-style switch statements
or expressions can have indented case blocks (as shown below):

switch (condition) {
    case ABC -> method("1");
    case DEF -> method("2");
    case XYZ -> method("3");
    default -> method("0");
}

However, the curent checkstyle.xml does not allow for this flexibility,
leading to a necessary checkstyleFail when there shouldn't be any.

Let's add checkstyle.xml rules that reflect this.

In Checkstyle's AST, SWITCH_RULE refers to the modern switch syntax
(case "A" ->), whereas the traditional switch syntax (case "A":) is
represented by a different node (typically SWITCH_GROUP).
